The Fixed Wing NEPT Service forms part of the NSW Health patient transport services and is intended to support the transfer of eligible patients in accordance with the NSW Health Service Specification for Non-Emergency Transport Providers (PD2024_008).

The proposed service model is anticipated to include:

- Provision of both fixed-wing air transport and road to transport non-emergency patients to and from locations including:
  - a place of residence (i.e. a private dwelling);
  - a nursing home or aged care facility;
  - a rehabilitation unit;
  - a hospice;
  - a public or private hospital; or
  - a correctional centre,
- Provision of a dedicated fleet of five (5) aircraft operating from a minimum of 2 bases, of which one is located within the Sydney Basin and the second regional location nominated by the tenderer.
- Provision of a fleet of road vehicles to conduct road transport at various locations in NSW.
- The clinical crew for the air transport component will be provided by NSW Ambulance while the clinical crew for the Road transport component would be supplied by the successful tenderer.

The information contained in this notice is indicative only and is subject to change. The publication of this notice does not constitute a commitment by HealthShare NSW or NSW Ambulance to proceed with any procurement process.
